# Run outputs are per-run artefacts, not source: a fresh replay writes one
# every time and committing them all would bury the ones that mean something.
runs/*
!.gitignore

# The committed runs. Task 01a14dce replaced every real name in the slices and
# prompts and re-recorded the cassettes; the eleven runs committed before it
# were removed from the tree because their rows, recorded answers and
# manifests carried real names and a LAN address. Their headline numbers are
# kept in README.md.
#
# The pre-public scrub then replaced the 102 negatives_102 rows (recorded
# producer removals) with synthetic stand-ins and re-keyed every cassette entry
# for them (see README "Synthetic negatives"). The runs below are one replay
# per committed cassette, written with no network. Every summary number in them
# equals the replay committed before the scrub: per-row predicted intent,
# demotion and its reason, error class and addressee outcome were compared row
# by row across all six configs and none moved. If a replay does not reproduce
# them, that is a finding about the harness to report, not a number to adjust.
!runs/20261026T201759Z-off_topic_default.json
!runs/20261026T201759Z-agent_roster_20260831.json
!runs/20261026T201759Z-binary_actionable.json
!runs/20261026T201759Z-broken_always_off_topic.json
!runs/20261026T201759Z-broken_malformed_schema.json
!runs/20261026T201759Z-broken_never_off_topic.json
